course: dictionary
lesson: 15909
title: Unnatural: not natural
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The start of «unnatural» is un-, which means not, as in unhappy and unfair. So unnatural means not natural. Natural things grow or happen by themselves, like rain or a tree, while unnatural things are made by people or are different from what usually happens in nature.
explain: «The room had an unnatural silence, as if everyone was holding their breath.» Silence is usually normal, but here it feels strange and odd, so unnatural means strange or not normal. The words around it give the clue.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The room had a strange silence» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Unnatural can also mean forced or false, like an unnatural voice that sounds fake, not relaxed.
fact: Un- at the start of a word often means not, as in unhappy and unfair.
fact: «Unnatural» means not natural: made by people, or different from what usually happens in nature.
fact: «Unnatural» can also mean strange, odd or not normal, as in «an unnatural glow».
fact: Unnatural colours in sweets often come from dyes, which are made by people.
fact: In a story, an unnatural silence or glow often tells the reader that something creepy is happening.
exercise: «The sweets had an unnatural bright blue colour.» What does unnatural mean here? | *Not natural, coloured by dyes made by people | Very tasty and sweet | Sticky and cold to touch | Fresh from the farm
exercise: In «unnatural», what does the start un- mean? | Before | *Not | Again | Very
exercise: «An unnatural glow came from the old house.» What does this suggest? | The house is brand new | It is a sunny day | *Something strange or odd is happening | The lights are very cheap
test: «Her laugh sounded unnatural, as if she was pretending.» What does unnatural suggest? | Very quick and sudden | Sweet and gentle | Loud and cheerful | *Forced and false, not relaxed
test: Which one is natural, not unnatural? | A dye-coloured sweet | A glowing sign made in a factory | *A tree growing in a forest | A made plastic toy
exam: «The unnatural silence made the children shiver.» What is the best meaning of unnatural here? | *Strange and not normal, a bit creepy | Very loud and noisy | Happy and bright | Made of soft wood
